{"kind":"artifact","text":"The MCP state tool's projection notes at f904524fb2520f037f9dcc50b33fed685bd3499a on request/mcp-projection-notes. A state result now carries a `projected` object saying how the fold read the act: its ruling when that is anything other than plain effect, any citation naming no event in this workroom, and for a report whether it became a review and which artifact it judges. Unknown body keys are still accepted, and docs/reference/mcp/state.md states both trade-offs — that describing rather than refusing keeps the body map open at the cost of stopping nothing, and that the notes are a report rather than a guarantee.","body":{"commit":"f904524fb2520f037f9dcc50b33fed685bd3499a","path":"request/mcp-projection-notes"}}